WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
Collagen is in your tendons,
skin, bone and artery walls.

2
00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.730
Pull on it, and it holds.

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.150
The protein that carries oxygen
in your blood is different.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.850
It dissolves inside red blood cells.

5
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.820
Yet both are just chains of amino acids.

6
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.780
So why is one tough as rope,
while the other dissolves?

7
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.940
In this mission, you'll
open up the blood protein:

8
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.900
four chains, each holding a
ring with iron at its centre.

9
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:30.210
Then you'll find out what
collagen is built to do.

10
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.120
Your mission: find out why
one protein is tough as rope,

11
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.710
while another dissolves.
